{"tool_name":"treesapp","contents":["biocontainers","oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biocontainers":{"name":"treesapp","identifiers":["doi:10.1093/bioinformatics/btaa588"],"license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"TreeSAPP is a functional and taxonomic annotation tool for microbial genomes and proteins","home_url":"https://github.com/hallamlab/TreeSAPP","keywords":["Genomics","Phylogenetics","Sequence Alignment","Genetics","Metagenome","Ortholog"],"manually_check":true,"total_pulls":32},"biotools":{"id":"treesapp","home":"https://github.com/hallamlab/TreeSAPP","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"the Tree-based Sensitive and Accurate Phylogenetic Profiler.\n\nIf you are working with a particularly complex reference package, from an orthologous group for example, or have extra phylogenetic information you'd like to include in your classifications, try annotating extra features with treesapp layer.","addition_date":"2021-01-18T09:53:06Z","last_update_date":"2021-03-04T08:48:24Z","biotools_curie":"biotools:treesapp","credit":[{"email":"shallam@mail.ubc.ca","name":"Steven J Hallam","typeEntity":"Person"},{"name":"Zachary Armstrong","typeEntity":"Person"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Query and retrieval","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0224"},{"term":"Regression analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3659"},{"term":"Taxonomic classification","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3460"}]}],"name":"TreeSAPP","owner":"zsmag19","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/BIOINFORMATICS/BTAA588","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2020 The Author(s) 2020. Published by Oxford University Press.Motivation: Microbial communities drive matter and energy transformations integral to global biogeochemical cycles, yet many taxonomic groups facilitating these processes remain poorly represented in biological sequence databases. Due to this missing information, taxonomic assignment of sequences from environmental genomes remains inaccurate. Results: We present the Tree-based Sensitive and Accurate Phylogenetic Profiler (TreeSAPP) software for functionally and taxonomically classifying genes, reactions and pathways from genomes of cultivated and uncultivated microorganisms using reference packages representing coding sequences mediating multiple globally relevant biogeochemical cycles. TreeSAPP uses linear regression of evolutionary distance on taxonomic rank to improve classifications, assigning both closely related and divergent query sequences at the appropriate taxonomic rank. TreeSAPP is able to provide quantitative functional and taxonomic classifications for both assembled and unassembled sequences and files supporting interactive tree of life visualizations.","authors":[{"name":"Armstrong Z."},{"name":"Chan K."},{"name":"Hallam S.J."},{"name":"McLaughlin R."},{"name":"Morgan-Lang C."},{"name":"Zhang G."}],"citationCount":1,"date":"2020-09-15T00:00:00Z","journal":"Bioinformatics","title":"TreeSAPP: The Tree-based Sensitive and Accurate Phylogenetic Profiler"},"pmcid":"PMC7695126","pmid":"32637989"}],"topic":[{"term":"Cladistics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3944"},{"term":"Metagenomics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3174"},{"term":"Molecular interactions, pathways and networks","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0602"},{"term":"Phylogenetics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3293"},{"term":"Sequence assembly","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0196"}]},"bioschemas":{"name":"TreeSAPP","home":"https://bio.tools/treesapp","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"the Tree-based Sensitive and Accurate Phylogenetic Profiler.\n\nIf you are working with a particularly complex reference package, from an orthologous group for example, or have extra phylogenetic information you'd like to include in your classifications, try annotating extra features with treesapp layer.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:tree